      "text": "The regular‑employment test says an employee is deemed regular when he is engaged to perform activities that are usually necessary or desirable in the employer’s usual business or trade, unless the work is limited to a specific project whose completion was set at hiring or is seasonal work for the season’s duration. Also, any employee who has rendered at least one year of service, whether continuous or broken, is considered regular with respect to that activity and continues as long as the activity exists.",
