      "component_id": "concern_002",
      "text": "The recorded test for regular employment provides that, despite any written or oral agreement to the contrary, an employee is regular when engaged to perform activities that are usually necessary or desirable in the employer’s usual business or trade, except when the job is fixed for a specific project whose termination was determined at engagement or is seasonal for the season’s length. Moreover, any employee who has completed at least one year of service, continuous or not, is deemed regular with respect to that activity and remains so while the activity exists.",
