      "text": "For a private construction employer, the key is to determine if the worker is hired for a specific project or a seasonal task whose completion date is set at hiring. When the job is project‑ or seasonal‑based, the employment is not automatically regular; it is treated as a project/seasonal arrangement. Only if the work is not so limited and involves activities usual to the employer’s business does it become regular; otherwise it is casual, and a worker with at least one year of service becomes regular for that activity.",
