      "text": "Under the Labor Code, ‘employer’ means any person or entity that hires workers, including private companies, government agencies, and non‑profit organizations. ‘Employee’ covers any individual who works for an employer. ‘Employment’ is defined as remunerative work performed for an employer, whether under a written or unwritten contract. A ‘job’ is the set of tasks assigned to a person, and a ‘task’ is a major element of work that produces a specific result.",
