      "text": "Under RA 7394 Art. 100, if a durable consumer product such as a rice cooker has an imperfection that is not fixed within the default thirty‑day period, the buyer may choose one of three remedies: a replacement with a like product in perfect condition, an immediate refund of the purchase price with monetary updating, or a proportionate reduction of the price. The thirty‑day deadline is only a default; the seller and buyer may agree to shorten it to at least seven days or extend it up to one hundred‑eighty days.",
      "evidence": [
