      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "Under the Consumer Act, the supplier of a durable product that has a quality defect—such as a broken chair height mechanism—is jointly liable for the imperfection. If the defect is not fixed within thirty days, the buyer may choose either a replacement of the same kind in perfect condition, a full refund with monetary updating, or a proportionate price reduction. The correction period may be adjusted but cannot be less than seven nor more than one hundred and eighty days, and the buyer may use the alternative remedies immediately when repairing the defect would further harm the product’s value.",
      "evidence": [
        { "quote_id": "concern_001.s1.q1" },
