      "text": "For a consumer who finds a product’s quality imperfect—like a chair with a broken height mechanism—the supplier is liable and must fix the defect. If the defect isn’t corrected within thirty days (which parties may adjust but not below seven nor above one hundred eighty days), the consumer can choose either a replacement of the same kind in perfect condition, a full refund with monetary updating, or a proportionate price reduction. Immediate use of these options is allowed when repairing would further harm the product’s value.",
