      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "Under the Omnibus Rules Implementing the Labor Code, wages must be paid at least once every two weeks or twice a month, so the interval between payments cannot exceed sixteen days, unless a force‑majeure event or circumstances beyond the employer’s control temporarily prevents payment, in which case the employer must pay immediately after the event ends.",
      "evidence": [
