    {
      "component_id": "concern_002",
      "text": "Republic Act No. 7394, Art. 81, makes it unlawful for a retailer to sell a consumer product without a visible price tag or label, and the selling price may not exceed the price shown on that tag. If the product is too small for a tag, a nearby price list may be used, and Art. 83 prohibits any erasures or alterations of the displayed price.",
