    {
      "component_id": "concern_002",
      "text": "Republic Act 10909 obliges a business to give the exact change in legal tender; it is unlawful to shortchange a consumer or to provide change in any form other than present currency. If a supermarket refuses the proper cash change, Department of Trade and Industry Order 16‑03 requires the establishment to pay the amount of change denied, in addition to any fine imposed.",
