{
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "An employer may deduct wages for loss or damage only if (a) the employee is clearly shown to be responsible, (b) the employee is given a reasonable chance to show cause why the deduction should not be made, (c) the amount is fair, reasonable and does not exceed the actual loss, and (d) the deduction does not surpass 20 percent of the employee’s weekly wages. The worker also has the right to answer the allegation and be heard before any deduction is effected.",
