      "text": "Under the Omnibus Rules, every employer must give each employee a rest period of at least 24 consecutive hours after six consecutive normal work days. An employer may only require an employee to work on that scheduled rest day when one of the emergencies or exceptional conditions listed in Section 6 (e.g., actual or impending disaster, urgent work to avoid loss, abnormal work pressure, prevention of loss of perishable goods, continuous‑seven‑day operations, or need for favorable weather) applies.",
