      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "For probationary hires, the law caps the probation period at six months when the work is not a learnable or apprenticeable job, and it obliges the employer to tell the employee at the start what standards must be met to become regular. If those standards were never explained, the employer has not complied with the statutory requirement.",
