      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "Under the Omnibus Rules, a worker may be dismissed only for a just or authorized cause and only after due process. Due process requires the employer to give a written notice stating the specific acts or omissions that justify dismissal, and the employee must be allowed a reasonable period to answer the allegations and be heard, with a representative if desired. Without these steps, the dismissal is not compliant.",
      "evidence": [
        { "quote_id": "concern_001.s1.q1" },
        { "quote_id": "concern_001.s2.q1" },
        { "quote_id": "concern_001.s3.q2" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "component_id": "concern_002",
      "text": "Republic Act 7394 makes a service supplier liable for any quality imperfection that renders the service improper or reduces its value. The consumer may choose among (1) having the service performed again at no extra cost, (2) an immediate refund of the amount paid with monetary updating, or (3) a proportionate price reduction. The supplier may also have a qualified third party redo the service at its own risk and cost.",
      "evidence": [
        { "quote_id": "concern_002.s1.q1" },
        { "quote_id": "concern_002.s1.q2" },
        { "quote_id": "concern_002.s1.q3" }
