      "component_id": "concern_002",
      "text": "Under RA 7394 Art. 68, a retailer is subsidiarily liable for a warranty when both the manufacturer and distributor fail to honor it, and must shoulder the expenses needed to honor the warranty. The buyer only has to present the warranty card or receipt to the immediate seller, and no other documents may be demanded. Therefore, a retailer may not refuse to accept the claim; it must forward the claim to the distributor at no cost to the consumer and can later pursue recovery from the distributor or manufacturer. The law does not prescribe a specific penalty for a retailer that refuses, leaving an enforcement gap.",
