      "text": "Under RA 7394 Art. 68, a retailer must accept the buyer’s warranty claim by presenting the warranty card or receipt to the immediate seller and cannot demand additional documents. If the manufacturer and distributor fail to honor the warranty, the retailer is subsidiarily liable and must shoulder the costs, though it may still pursue the distributor or manufacturer. The law therefore obliges the retailer to take the claim to the distributor at no cost to you. The statute does not spell out a specific remedy when a retailer outright refuses to accept the claim, leaving that gap to be addressed through consumer‑protection agencies.",
