{
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "For a private employer to deduct cash from an employee’s wages, the deduction is only lawful if (1) the employee is clearly shown to be responsible for the loss, (2) the employee is given a reasonable chance to explain why the deduction should not be made, (3) the amount deducted is fair, reasonable and does not exceed the actual loss, and (4) the deduction does not exceed 20 % of the employee’s weekly wages, and the practice must be recognized in the employer’s trade. Absent those conditions, any withholding of wages without the worker’s consent is unlawful.",
