      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "Under PD 442 Art. 116, it is unlawful for any person to withhold any part of a worker’s wages without the worker’s consent. The Omnibus Rules (Section 14) permit a deduction for loss or damage only if (a) the employee is clearly shown to be responsible, (b) the employee is given a reasonable chance to contest it, (c) the amount is fair, reasonable and does not exceed the actual loss, and (d) the deduction does not exceed 20 % of the employee’s weekly wages. Without meeting those conditions, deducting missing cash from everyone would violate the wage‑withholding prohibition.",
