      "text": "Republic Act 10909 Sec. 4 declares it unlawful for any business to shortchange a consumer, even a small amount, and requires the establishment to give the exact change without waiting for the consumer to ask. If the establishment fails, DTI Administrative Order 16‑03 Sec. 2 provides that, besides any fine, the establishment must pay the complainant the total amount of change that was not given, as determined by a DTI audit.",
