      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "Under the Labor Code, an employee is regular when engaged in activities that are usual or desirable for the employer’s business, unless the job is for a specific project or is seasonal (Art. 295). If the employee works beyond the probationary period, he is deemed regular (Omnibus Rules Sec. 5(c)). The probationary period itself may not exceed six months when the work is not learnable or apprenticeable (Sec. 6(b)). Even a casual employee who has rendered at least one year of service becomes regular for that activity (Art. 295).",
      "evidence": [
        { "quote_id": "concern_001.s1.q4" },
        { "quote_id": "concern_001.s1.q5" },
        { "quote_id": "concern_001.s1.q7" }        
