    {
      "component_id": "concern_002",
      "text": "The Consumer Act requires that a repair service be performed with adequate, new or original parts that meet the manufacturer’s specifications unless the buyer expressly allows otherwise (Art. 103). If the repair is not completed within thirty days, the consumer may choose a replacement, a full reimbursement with monetary updating, or a proportional price reduction (Art. 100). The retailer, as the immediate seller, must accept the warranty claim without extra documents and may be held subsidiarily liable if the distributor or manufacturer fails to honor the warranty (Art. 68, retail provision).",
      "evidence": [
        { "quote_id": "concern_002.s2.q1" },
