      "text": "For a private‑office employee on probation, the rules say the probationary period may not exceed six (6) months when the work is not learnable or apprenticeable; the employer must tell the employee at hiring what standards will be used to decide regularization; the employee can be dismissed only for a just cause or for failing to meet those reasonable standards; and once the probation ends and the employee is allowed to keep working, he is deemed a regular employee.",
